پیشرفت tutee نقشی در تمرین مدل ندارد میشود سیستمی پیاده کرد که تاثیر روی تصمیم به توضیح بیشتر و یا قرارگیری آن بذارد

3) Add “placebo” controls to show it’s not just “extra reward”

Two very convincing controls:

Control A: Random tutee policy

Same environment + tutee actions exist

but the tutee action is chosen randomly (or at fixed frequency)

If your learned policy beats random, you show:

“Benefit comes from learning when to use it, not from always having it.”

Control B: Shuffled/neutral bonus

Keep an action that gives the same average bonus magnitude, but make it independent of mastery regime (or shuffled across steps/topics)

If your real tutee mechanism beats the neutral bonus, you show:

“The structure (desirable difficulty / readiness) matters, not just injecting extra mastery.”